  var contexts = {
    "CFM": "\n/* ==================== FILE: cfm-capabilities.md ==================== */\n---\n\n## id: card-cfm-cap-001 title: \"OSTTRA Cash Flow Management (CFM) Capabilities & Technical Perimeter\" category: \"capability\\_card\" portfolio\\_status: \"active\\_core\" claim\\_status: \"shipped\" commercial\\_lead: \"Tom Woolfenden\" distribution: \"client\\_facing\" first\\_defence\\_approver: \"John Kenchington\" last\\_reviewed: 2026-10-27 validation\\_status: \"unvalidated\\_baseline\" governance: chinese\\_wall\\_verified: true editorial\\_lint: \"passed\" git\\_commit: \"c8ae608\" body\\_sha256: \"cc0108ed9d273c68abbc35e9daf1b67de75531eddcfb6b92e6a375645a42e0ef\"\n\n# OSTTRA Cash Flow Management (CFM) — Product Capabilities & Perimeter\n\n*Domain: 01\\_Product\\_Capabilities \\| Knowledge Hub Reference \\| Multi-Tenant Institutional Card* *Product: OSTTRA Cash Flow Management (CFM)* *Commercial Lead: Tom Woolfenden*\n\n---\n\n> \\[\\!WARNING\\] **Validation Status: Unvalidated Baseline** This content represents an initial structural baseline compiled from historical documentation and unverified telemetry. It is pending formal QBR validation and sign-off by the Commercial Lead and PMM. Do not cite client commitments or roadmap dates externally until validated.\n\n## 1\\. Core Functional Essence (Block 1\\)\n\n### What the Product Does\n\nOSTTRA Cash Flow Management (CFM) is a centralised multi-party workflow platform that enables market participants to compare, affirm, net, and settle periodic lifecycle cashflows across OTC derivatives, Equities, Fixed Income, FX, and Securities Lending.\n\n- **Bilateral Matching Engine:** Ingests cashflow records and automatically compares them on a 1-to-1 or 1-to-many basis against counterparty submissions, evaluating payment dates, amounts, currencies, and direction.  \n- **GUI Affirmation Workflow:** Provides a lightweight click-to-accept or click-to-reject web portal for counterparties without automated API connectivity, removing the need for bilateral bilateral spreadsheet exchanges.  \n- **Lifecycle Status Tracking:** Tracks cashflow records through their complete lifecycle, dynamically updating items from \"Projected\" to \"Fixed / Ready to Settle\" as fixing dates pass.  \n- **Configurable Bilateral Netting:** Automatically calculates agreed gross-to-net settlement positions per counterparty and currency bucket, preserving complete audit lineage back to individual gross records.  \n- **Settlement Instruction Dispatch:** Generates verified ISO 20022 and SWIFT MT payment messages (MT202, MT103) directly to custodian banks and payment systems upon matching/affirmation.  \n- **Independent Third-Party Calculation:** Ingests golden-source trade confirmations (from MarkitWire and EPS) to calculate expected cashflow amounts independently, isolating whether disputes originate from trade terms or payment calculations.\n\n### Operational Scope & Integration Boundaries\n\n- **Settlement Instruction Dispatch:** Normalises, matches, and nets cashflow payments, creating and dispatching verified settlement instructions (MT202/pacs.009) to client settlement banks and custodians who execute the actual fund movements.  \n- **Post-Trade Lifecycle Focus:** Operates strictly on affirmed trades, resets, and payment obligations; trade capture and legal confirmation occur upstream in systems like MarkitWire or CCP Connect.  \n- **Bilateral Netting Infrastructure:** Provides multilateral netting and bilateral pairing, calculating netted settlement obligations without assuming central counterparty credit risk.\n\n---\n\n## 2\\. Coverage & Technical Connectivity (Block 2\\)\n\n### Supported Asset Classes & 70+ ISITC Payment Types\n\n- **OTC Derivatives:** Bilateral Interest Rate Swaps (IRS), Credit Default Swaps (CDS), Total Return Swaps (TRS) periodic coupons, resets, and upfront fees.  \n- **Equity Derivatives:** Equity Portfolio Swaps (EPS), CFD resets, dividend adjustments, and financing legs.  \n- **Fixed Income:** TBA pair-offs, coupon payments, reclaims, and bond interest.  \n- **Foreign Exchange:** Non-CLS bilateral FX cash flows and fees.  \n- **Securities Lending:** Manufactured dividends/income, borrow/loan fees, and collateral interest.  \n- **Collateral & Margin:** Interest payments on cash and non-cash collateral.\n\n### Currency Scope\n\n- **20 Settlement Currencies Supported Natively:** Multi-currency netting buckets with custom operational cut-off times per currency.\n\n### Ingest & Connectivity Protocols\n\n- **API & Messaging:** Real-time REST API, FIX protocol, CSV batch file ingest, XML messaging.  \n- **SWIFT Network:** ISO 20022 MX messages and ISO 15022 MT settlement messaging.  \n- **OSTTRA Network Interconnections:** MarkitWire / EPS (trade economics golden source), triResolve (portfolio reconciliation and dispute drill-downs), triCalculate (independent valuation verification).\n\n---\n\n## 3\\. Plain-English Operational Walkthrough\n\n### How the Workflow Operates in Practice\n\n1. **Periodic Cashflow Ingestion:**  \n   - Ingests upcoming periodic lifecycle cashflows (coupons, resets, fees, manufactured dividends) via real-time REST API, FIX, or batch CSV.  \n   - Normalises cashflow records across 70+ ISITC payment types into a standardised multi-asset data model.  \n2. **Automated 1-to-1 and 1-to-Many Matching:**  \n   - Evaluates incoming cashflow records against counterparty submissions, comparing payment dates, net amounts, currencies, and direction.  \n   - Supports 1-to-many matching where a single counterparty payment corresponds to multiple underlying trade cashflow items.  \n3. **Web GUI Affirmation Blotter:**  \n   - Counterparties without dedicated API integrations access a lightweight, secure web portal to review, affirm, or dispute alleged cashflow amounts with a single click.  \n   - Eliminates manual bilateral email trails and spreadsheet reconciliation.  \n4. **Lifecycle Status Progression:**  \n   - Dynamically tracks cashflow items from \"Projected\" to \"Fixed / Ready to Settle\" as floating rate fixings, corporate action announcements, or financing rates are locked in.  \n5. **Configurable Bilateral Netting:**  \n   - Aggregates agreed cashflows into multi-currency net settlement obligations per counterparty and value date.  \n   - Preserves complete audit traceability back to each underlying gross trade ticket, reducing settlement transaction volume by up to 80%.  \n6. **Settlement Instruction Dispatch:**  \n   - Automatically generates and transmits verified ISO 20022 and SWIFT MT messages (MT202, MT103) directly to custodian banks and settlement agents.  \n7. **Cross-Product Break Resolution:**  \n   - Disputed cashflows link directly into OSTTRA Resolve (for portfolio valuation discrepancy drill-downs) and MarkitWire (for legal trade confirmation term verification).\n\n---\n\n## 4\\. Supporting Information & Domain Concepts\n\n- **70+ ISITC Cash Flow Codes:** Comprehensive industry-standard payment categorisation spanning swap resets, periodic coupons, upfront fees, CFD financing, TBA pair-offs, and securities lending borrow fees.  \n- **1-to-Many Matching:** The ability to match a single aggregated payment claim from one counterparty against multiple discrete underlying cashflows on the other, resolving complex multi-account settlements without manual calculations.  \n- **Gross-to-Net Netting Sets:** Configurable rules that consolidate dozens of bilateral payment obligations across currencies and accounts into single net payment amounts, dramatically lowering SWIFT messaging and bank settlement fees.  \n- **Margin in Transit Gap:** The operational timing gap where agreed lifecycle cashflows settle 1 – 2 days after calculation, creating temporary uncollateralised exposures that inflate Variation Margin requirements; CFM aligns cashflow affirmation directly with margin processes.  \n- **Fixing vs Projected Resets:** Projected cashflows represent estimated future obligations based on forward curves; Fixing cashflows become definitive once official benchmark rates (SOFR, SONIA, EURIBOR) or corporate dividends are fixed.\n\n\n/* ==================== FILE: cfm-narrative.md ==================== */\n---\n\n## id: card-cfm-nar-001 title: \"OSTTRA Cash Flow Management (CFM) Narrative & Roadmaps\" category: \"narrative\\_card\" portfolio\\_status: \"active\\_core\" claim\\_status: \"roadmap\" commercial\\_lead: \"Tom Woolfenden\" distribution: \"client\\_facing\" first\\_defence\\_approver: \"John Kenchington\" last\\_reviewed: 2026-10-27 validation\\_status: \"unvalidated\\_baseline\" governance: chinese\\_wall\\_verified: true editorial\\_lint: \"passed\" git\\_commit: \"c8ae608\" body\\_sha256: \"12564a63df1956828effd915b460fee83636f047f32b0740f589241d8efca8b4\"\n\n# OSTTRA Cash Flow Management (CFM) — Narrative, Value Proposition & Roadmap\n\n*Domain: 02\\_Narrative\\_and\\_Roadmaps \\| Knowledge Hub Reference \\| Multi-Tenant Institutional Card* *Product: OSTTRA Cash Flow Management (CFM)* *Commercial Lead: Tom Woolfenden*\n\n---\n\n> \\[\\!WARNING\\] **Validation Status: Unvalidated Baseline** This content represents an initial structural baseline compiled from historical documentation and unverified telemetry. It is pending formal QBR validation and sign-off by the Commercial Lead and PMM. Do not cite client commitments or roadmap dates externally until validated.\n\n## 1\\. Executive Narrative & Market Driver\n\n### The Strategic Problem\n\nAcross capital markets, periodic cashflows arising from open trades and lifecycle events are still routinely coordinated through fragmented manual processes: unstructured emails, bilateral spreadsheets, and phone chases. As global settlement timelines compress (T+1 settlement across jurisdictions) and funding cut-offs tighten, this operational friction becomes critical:\n\n- **Late Agreement & Payment Fails:** Unresolved discrepancies close to value date result in failed payments, overdraft charges, and costly interest claims.  \n- **Liquidity Drag:** Settling on an un-netted gross basis inflates transaction costs and ties up valuable intraday liquidity.  \n- **The \"Margin in Transit\" Gap:** The operational separation between lifecycle cashflows and Variation Margin (VM) creates timing gaps and funding inefficiencies.\n\n### The OSTTRA Value Proposition\n\nOSTTRA Cash Flow Management (CFM) replaces bilateral manual chasing with an automated, multi-party hub to compare, affirm, net, and settle lifecycle cashflows across 70+ ISITC types. By connecting cashflows directly to validated trade records and consensus reconciliation, CFM eliminates manual breaks, cuts settlement costs, and releases liquidity.\n\n---\n\n## 2\\. Institutional Proof Points\n\n- **70+ ISITC Cash Flow Types:** Production coverage across OTC, Equities, Fixed Income, FX, and Securities Lending.  \n- **20 Global Settlement Currencies:** Thousands of live transactions processed across Tier-1 banks and asset managers.  \n- **Up to 80% Reduction in Settlement Messages:** Automated bilateral netting sets compress gross transaction volume into net settlement figures, driving major savings on SWIFT fees and bank charges.\n\n---\n\n## 3\\. Product Horizon & Delivery Commitments\n\n### Now `[shipped]` (Production Capabilities)\n\n- **Multi-Asset Cashflow Ingestion & Matching:** Production matching engine across OTC, CFD, Collateral Interest, and Securities Lending `[shipped]`.  \n- **GUI Click-to-Accept Portal:** Zero-integration web interface enabling non-API counterparties to affirm or reject alleged cashflows `[shipped]`.  \n- **Configurable Bilateral Netting:** Automated netting sets by counterparty and currency bucket with full underlying gross lineage `[shipped]`.  \n- **Direct SWIFT Settlement Instruction Dispatch:** Automated generation and delivery of outbound settlement instructions to payment custodians `[shipped]`.\n\n### Next `[roadmap]` (In Development)\n\n- **OSTTRA Independent Trade Economics Calculation:** Ingestion of MarkitWire trade confirmations to calculate and display expected cashflows independently, isolating whether breaks stem from trade terms or payment calculations `[roadmap]`.  \n- **Automated Rule-Based Cashflow Rejection:** Customisable business rules to auto-reject mismatched cashflows falling outside agreed tolerance thresholds `[roadmap]`.  \n- **Bilateral Currency Cut-Off Management:** Automated enforcement of counterparty- and currency-specific operational cut-off times to protect payment release windows `[roadmap]`.  \n- **Enhanced Exception & Dispute Workflows:** Advanced break categorisation with drill-downs into upstream portfolio reconciliation and trade records `[roadmap]`.  \n- **Unified Ecosystem SSO:** Single sign-on extension bridging CFM with adjacent OSTTRA applications (triResolve, OTM) `[roadmap]`.\n\n### Later `[vision]` (Strategic Horizon)\n\n- **Cashflow-to-VM Margin Alignment:** Side-by-side synchronisation of agreed periodic cashflows with agreed Variation Margin (VM) calls to eliminate the 1-day \"margin in transit\" gap and reduce funding buffer costs `[vision]`.  \n- **AI Dispute & Diagnostic Analytics:** Machine learning pattern recognition to detect recurring break drivers (e.g., day-count conventions, floating rate index fixing discrepancies) and suggest automated fixes `[vision]`.  \n- **Digital & Tokenised Cashflow Settlement:** Exploratory interoperability research for emerging digital and tokenised settlement rails, subject to institutional market adoption `[vision]`.\n\n\n/* ==================== FILE: osttra-acronyms.md ==================== */\n---\n\n## id: doc-acronyms-001 title: \"OSTTRA Master Acronyms & Terminology Glossary\" category: \"glossary\" portfolio\\_status: \"active\\_core\" claim\\_status: \"shipped\" commercial\\_lead: \"Nathan Ondyak\" first\\_defence\\_approver: \"John Kenchington\" last\\_reviewed: 2026-10-26 validation\\_status: \"unvalidated\\_baseline\" governance: chinese\\_wall\\_verified: true editorial\\_lint: \"passed\" git\\_commit: \"c8ae608\" body\\_sha256: \"975c44cd7c1443f23d4d93715387f284f844cf7993aea930cd1d3f64c4273407\"\n\n# OSTTRA Acronyms & Proprietary Glossary\n\n*Knowledge Hub Reference \\| Single Source of Truth for Enterprise & Market Terminology* *Scope: 39 Proprietary Technologies & 96 Standard Financial Market Terms (135 Total)*\n\n---\n\n## 1\\. Proprietary Technology & Internal Projects (Table 1\\)\n\n| Term / Acronym | Applicable Asset Classes | Full Name / Description | Functional Benefit |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| **Alpine** | Infrastructure / Cross-Asset | Unified Onboarding. | The central orchestration layer for the OSTTRA ecosystem. It facilitates digital onboarding for new clients, reverse onboarding for existing clients, and integrates with third-party platforms (e.g., Saphyre, OA) to provide a single source of truth for static data. |\n| **Apigee / Apigee X** | Infrastructure / Cross-Asset | OSTTRA's chosen API Gateway and centralised API hosting platform built on GCP technology. | Provides a single entry point for API exposure, standardising security (authentication/authorisation), traffic management (rate/quota limiting), and monetisation. |\n| **CCPC FX (or CCPC)** | FX | OSTTRA's proprietary Central Counterparty Clearing connectivity platform/module. | Supports messaging and automated workflows required by participants involved in central clearing (including block-level and client clearing). |\n| **CFM (Cash Flow Management)** | Equities, Cross-Asset | OSTTRA's market utility for pre-agreement settlement orchestration across all asset classes / Cash Flow Management platform. | Acts as a centralised hub to view, affirm, and net alleged cashflows across over 70 ISITC cashflow types across all asset classes, feeding confirmed flows directly to internal payment systems for automated STP settlement. |\n| **CRDS (Client Reference Data Services)** | FX, Equities | Client Reference Data Services (CRDS). | A single, authoritative source of truth for customer reference data. It eliminates the need for siloed management layers by providing a self-service platform with built-in auditing, reporting, and 4-eyes checks for Traiana products and new services (such as Equity Swaps). |\n| **CreditLink** | FX | OSTTRA CreditLink is Traiana's real-time credit monitoring and control service for the tri-party brokerage community. | Serves as the trusted credit-risk management engine for FX prime brokerage. It provides real-time visibility into credit limit utilisation and an ultra-low latency credit \"kill switch\". |\n| **Developer Portal** | Infrastructure / Cross-Asset | OSTTRA's external centralised API catalogue (developer.osttra.com), built using Drupal. | Hosts API documentation and sandbox environments for prospects to explore APIs without an active subscription, integrating with Salesforce for lead generation. |\n| **DMS (including DMS Daas)** | FX | OSTTRA's proprietary core data management and enablement system. | Integrates core trade data with dashboards to provide clients with insights into key performance metrics across Rates, Credit, and Equities. |\n| **DNM** | FX | Designation Notice Manager. | A legacy Traiana service that helps FX Prime Brokers establish, monitor, amend, and terminate FX Tri-Party agreements. |\n| **Docubot (or Dot)** | FX | Dot (DocuBot) is OSTTRA's proprietary digital assistance tool. | Enables employees and clients to quickly search and retrieve technical documentation. |\n| **ELC** | Infrastructure / Cross-Asset | Externalisation Lifecycle. | The operational framework used to build an end-to-end proxy setup, allowing internal services to be securely published as APIs on the public internet. |\n| **EM (Software)** | Rates, Credit | Exception Management (EM) is a proprietary project module managed within OSTTRA's CSM portfolio. | Designed to provide automated exception workflows to highlight cash flow breaks and discrepancies. |\n| **Equity Portfolio Swaps** | Equities | OSTTRA's post-trade management programme spanning T0 and T+ lifecycles for prime-brokered equity swaps. | Brings end-to-end visibility and post-trade transparency across lifecycle management, reconciliation, and settlements. |\n| **OSTTRA Connect for ETD (ClientLink)** | Equities, ETD | OSTTRA Connect middle-office allocation matching and clearing platform for exchange-traded derivatives (formerly ETD ClientLink). | Coordinates client trade allocation instructions and returns real-time clearing statuses, solving the \"IMC blindspot\". |\n| **FX PvP Settlement (Diamond PvP)** | FX | OSTTRA's bilateral settlement orchestration service backed by Baton Systems and DLT technology. | Provides on-demand, intra-day netting and settlement orchestration to mitigate Herstatt risk and optimise liquidity. |\n| **Jigsaw** | FX, Equities, Post-Trade | OSTTRA's proprietary central data storage and enablement platform. | Facilitates the central storage of live positions and enables bulk generation of cashflows and valuations across downstream post-trade lifecycle systems. |\n| **JRDS** | Infrastructure / Cross-Asset | Jigsaw Reference Data Store / Service. | The central identity management translator. It stores unique IDs for institutions, users, and entities, enabling cross-platform identity validation and data interoperability without enforcing rigid centralisation. |\n| **LimitHub** | Post-Trade | OSTTRA's centralised limit checking and pre-trade clearing certainty platform. | Provides clearing brokers and clients with real-time visibility of credit limit utilisation consolidated across multiple venues. |\n| **OSTTRA Connect for Rates (MarkitWire)** | Rates, Credit | OSTTRA Connect trade processing, confirmation, and affirmation platform for OTC interest rate derivatives and credit derivatives (MarkitWire). | Serves as the core post-trade processing engine and central repository for OTC derivatives transactions. |\n| **OSTTRA Connect for FXPB (Message Center)** | FX | OSTTRA Connect messaging middleware and GUI system designed to normalise, transform, and route transaction data for FX prime brokerage (Message Center). | Automates the matching, affirmation, and allocation workflows by translating complex message formats. |\n| **NetLink** | FX | Traiana's proprietary rules-based FX netting and aggregation system. | Drives trading efficiency by aggregating and netting FX transactions, with secondary support for incidental post-trade connectivity and routing. |\n| **ODC** | FX | OSTTRA Documentation Centre. | A document store for prime-brokerage agreements that govern trading arrangements such as give-ups. It extends and replaces the legacy capabilities of DNM. |\n| **OSTTRA API Hub** | Infrastructure / Cross-Asset | OSTTRA's cohesive API ecosystem. | A central platform for developing, managing, and utilising APIs internally and externally, decoupling consumers from backend services to minimise downtime. |\n| **OSTTRA Digital Assistant** | Equities, Post-Trade | OSTTRA's natural language documentation assistant. | Allows clients to search and interrogate UI documentation in real time, automatically routing unresolved queries to the IT Service Desk. |\n| **OSTTRA Reset** | Post-Trade | OSTTRA's portfolio basis risk reduction service (formerly Reset). | Enables traders to offset basis risks by holding multilateral matching sessions and generating risk-offsetting trades. |\n| **OTM** | Cross-Asset | OSTTRA Trade Manager. | The consolidated User Interface (UI) for MarkitSERV platform services, supporting cross-asset trade management. |\n| **PRF** | Cross-Asset | Product Refinement Forum. | Collaborative product and engineering forums where the development pipeline, sprint backlogs, and roadmap adjustments are worked out across shared platforms (e.g. MarkitWire). |\n| **SSO** | FX, Infrastructure | Single Sign-On. | OSTTRA's integrated authentication service secured via Microsoft Entra. |\n| **OSTTRA Connect for FX (TradeServ FX)** | FX | OSTTRA Connect cloud-based post-trade processing, confirmation, and lifecycle platform for FX transactions (TradeServ FX). | Acts as a core platform for processing FX transaction data and facilitating real-time validated data feeds. |\n| **TradeSTP / FX BA / SignalHub** | FX | OSTTRA's proprietary FX straight-through processing system, FX Business Analytics (FX BA), and SignalHub. | Enables a fully automated, end-to-end post-trade workflow from execution down to settlement without manual intervention, backed by commercial business analytics. |\n| **OSTTRA Rebalance (formerly triBalance)** | FX, Post-Trade | OSTTRA's portfolio rebalancing service (formerly triBalance). | Reduces credit risk, bilateral MTM exposure, and initial margin (IM) requirements by rebalancing portfolios. |\n| **OSTTRA Calculate (formerly triCalculate)** | FX, Post-Trade | OSTTRA's high-performance valuation, risk, and XVA analytics engine (formerly triCalculate). | Generates exposure profiles, XVA sensitivities, and pre-deal margin/risk checks for OTC derivatives. |\n| **OSTTRA Margin (formerly triResolve Margin / triMargin)** | Post-Trade | OSTTRA's end-to-end collateral management and margin process service (formerly triResolve Margin / triMargin). | Automates the margin call lifecycle across cleared and uncleared OTC derivatives. |\n| **OSTTRA Reduce (formerly triReduce)** | FX, Post-Trade | OSTTRA's multilateral portfolio compression service (formerly triReduce). | Enables market participants to compress and eliminate gross notional exposure and line items without altering market risk. |\n| **OSTTRA Resolve (formerly triResolve)** | FX, Post-Trade | OSTTRA's market-standard portfolio reconciliation and dispute management service (formerly triResolve). | Reconciles client positions, balances, and margin call workflows against clearing broker data to mitigate risk. |\n| **TRM** | FX | Trading Relationship Management. | Traiana's legacy solution suite for integrating counterparties, automating trade processes, and managing trading relationships in FX. |\n| **TRV (Trade Record & Valuations)** | Post-Trade | Trade Record & Valuations project. | Delivers projected cash flows, PV, and risk data on a trade-by-trade basis for MarkitWire's non-cleared Rates trade data. |\n| **UDO (Unified Digital Onboarding)** | FX | Unified Digital Onboarding (UDO) is OSTTRA's proprietary onboarding enabler system. | Automates and streamlines the customer onboarding process, supporting strategic growth initiatives. |\n\n---\n\n## 2\\. Standard Financial Market Terms & Instruments (Table 2\\)\n\n| Market Acronym | Applicable Asset Classes | Standard Financial Meaning |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| **ABAC** | Infrastructure | Attribute-Based Access Control (A security model that evaluates attributes or characteristics to determine access rights). |\n| **AI** | Equities | Artificial Intelligence (The application of advanced algorithms to automate trade matching and exception predictions). |\n| **API** | FX | Application Programming Interface (A software intermediary that allows two financial applications to interact). |\n| **APS** | Equities | Advanced Portfolio System (A third-party portfolio management service integrated via FIS). |\n| **AWS** | Equities | Amazon Web Services (A comprehensive, highly secure cloud computing platform used for infrastructure hosting). |\n| **BBG** | Equities | Bloomberg (The industry-standard global financial news, data analytics, and ticker symbology identifier platform). |\n| **BI** | Equities | Business Intelligence (The applications and processes used to analyse datasets and present actionable metrics to clients). |\n| **Block** | FX | Block Trade (A large-scale transaction or order executed outside open market venues to minimise price impact). |\n| **BRL** | Rates, Credit, Post-Trade | Brazilian Real (The official fiat currency of Brazil). |\n| **Bullion** | FX | Precious Metals (Physical gold, silver, platinum,